  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A long straight wire carries a current <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span>. What is the correct expression for the magnitude of the magnetic field at a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> from the wire?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{\\mu _0 I}{4\\pi r^2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{\\mu_0 I}{2\\pi r}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{\\mu_0 I}{4\\pi r}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\dfrac{\\mu_0 I^2}{4\\pi r}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
